TASK FEAT77
	TITLE "Locate every validation issue in a way a repair can act on"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "every issue the validator reports names the section it concerns, and the ones bearing on"
		+ "one entry name that entry in a single index space, whichever code they carry"
	SPEC "an issue bearing on one field names that field as a value of its own, and not only inside"
		+ "the sentence shown on screen"
	SPEC "a float serialization issue and a unique host issue each name the entry they concern,"
		+ "where today they name nothing"
	SPEC "the sentences the command line and the save manager display for an invalid save are"
		+ "unchanged"
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "A fix the user ticks has to be applied to one entry of one section, and today an"
		+ "issue cannot say which. The two codes that carry an entryIndex do not count in the same"
		+ "space: the unreadable line carries its rank among the lines of the section, the schema"
		+ "violation its rank among the readable entries alone, so one unreadable line above a"
		+ "violation shifts every index below it and a repair would rewrite the wrong entry. The"
		+ "field is only present inside the detail sentence, which presentation treats as opaque"
		+ "text. The float serialization and unique host checks carry no location at all, the first"
		+ "because it scans the raw text and the second because it counts across the whole players"
		+ "section. Nothing here changes what the validator accepts or refuses, so the single"
		+ "source of warnings stays one source and the four flows keep their verdict; only the"
		+ "shape of an issue grows. This is the precondition of the fix catalogue and of everything"
		+ "the rest of the wave applies"
		REF @COMMAND.ValidateSave
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.ASectionLineIsOneJsonEntry
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: its wave 7 tasks are rejected; the"
		+ "repair rests on the existing validator, detects the defects of the save, presents a"
		+ "table of fixes to tick and writes a new save file on confirmation"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the unreadable line carries the rank of the"
		+ "line in its section and the schema violation the rank of the entry among the readable"
		+ "ones, the field name sits inside the detail sentence as the instance path of the schema"
		+ "error, and the float serialization and unique host issues carry neither section nor"
		+ "entry"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping

TASK FEAT78
	TITLE "Propose the fixes that repair a save the validator rejects"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "a save the validator rejects yields a plan listing, for each proposed fix, the issues it"
		+ "resolves, what the save carries before and what it will carry after, whether the fix"
		+ "discards data, and whether it can be left out or comes with any rewritten file"
	SPEC "a defect for which no fix is known appears in the plan as not repairable automatically,"
		+ "and never disappears from it"
	SPEC "a save the validator accepts yields a plan proposing no fix"
	SPEC "a save whose section count is unsupported yields a plan saying so and saying that no"
		+ "other defect could be looked for"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT77
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "The table the user confirms is this plan, so the plan is built before any UI exists"
		+ "and is tested without one. Building it needs the sections of a save the validator"
		+ "rejects, which no use case exposes today: display and merge both return before calling"
		+ "the parser when validation fails, while the parser itself never refuses a save, records"
		+ "the lines it cannot read and returns every other one. The plan therefore reads the"
		+ "issues from the validator, the single source, and the sections from the parser, and"
		+ "pairs them; it invents no detection of its own. Two defects need no fix code at all, the"
		+ "unreadable line being already dropped by the parser and the float suffix being already"
		+ "written back by the serializer, which is why the plan is worth its own task before"
		+ "anything is applied. A defect with no known fix stays visible: a repair that hides what"
		+ "it cannot mend is worse than one that mends nothing"
		REF @COMMAND.ValidateSave
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @TASK.FEAT77
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
		REF @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the defects of the save are detected by"
		+ "the existing validator and presented as a table of the fixes to apply, the user ideally"
		+ "ticking which ones"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the parser records an unreadable line and"
		+ "continues, the display and merge use cases call it only after a valid verdict, and the"
		+ "entry serializer writes the dot zero suffix back for the twelve float fields the check"
		+ "scans"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing

TASK FEAT79
	TITLE "Write a new save file applying the fixes the caller selected"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "applying a selection of fixes produces new save content, leaves the content it was given"
		+ "untouched, and reports the validation of the result"
	SPEC "the fixes the rewrite itself carries are applied whatever the selection, and the result"
		+ "lists them"
	SPEC "the result names the issues that remain and the selected fixes that could not be applied,"
		+ "each with its reason"
	SPEC "a player identifier beyond the range of a double comes out of the repair as the same"
		+ "decimal text it went in with"
	SPEC "a save carrying the legacy twelve part format comes out in the eleven section format, and"
		+ "the result says that the terrain layers are not carried over"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT78
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "This is where the repair writes. The whole result is produced by parsing the"
		+ "rejected save, applying the selected fixes to the parsed sections and serializing them"
		+ "again, so the two defects the round trip already mends cost no fix code and the third,"
		+ "several host players, is a single assignment on the players section. Serializing is what"
		+ "makes the repair risky rather than the fixes: the entry serializer refuses a nested"
		+ "value, so a save whose corruption is a nested field cannot be written at all and has to"
		+ "come back as a named failure instead of a thrown error; the identifier of a player is"
		+ "written as its exact decimal text and must not be parsed into a number on the way"
		+ "through; and the serializer writes ten sections, so a legacy save is converted whether"
		+ "or not the user asked. The result is validated again before it is handed back, exactly"
		+ "as the merge validates its own output, and what remains is reported rather than"
		+ "swallowed"
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @RULE.ASaveHasElevenSectionsTheLastReservedAndEmpty
		REF @RULE.APlayerEntryCarriesCameraViewAndItsLifetimeTotals
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @SECTION.Reserved
		REF @TASK.FEAT78
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: on confirmation a new save file is"
		+ "created carrying the corrections, the file loaded being never overwritten"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the merge use case validates the content it"
		+ "has just serialized before presenting it, the entry serializer throws on a nested field,"
		+ "and the round trip of an int64 player identifier is covered by the serializer"
		+ "specification"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing

TASK FEAT80
	TITLE "Repair a rejected save from the save manager"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "loading a save the validator rejects shows, besides its errors, the defects grouped by"
		+ "kind with the fix proposed for each; a fix that can be left out carries a box to tick,"
		+ "and a fix any rewritten file carries is shown as always applied, with what it discards"
	SPEC "a defect for which no fix is proposed is shown as such, with the entry it concerns and no"
		+ "box"
	SPEC "confirming downloads a new file under a name distinct from the loaded one, and shows what"
		+ "the validator still reports about it"
	SPEC "a save whose section count is unsupported shows the one defect it produces and no repair"
		+ "to confirm"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT79
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT70
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "Today a rejected save ends the page: the route shows the list of validation messages"
		+ "and nothing else, and the visualization area stays empty. The repair view takes that"
		+ "dead end and turns it into the table the user acts on, reusing the export path the wave"
		+ "before builds so that the corrected save leaves as a new file and the loaded one is"
		+ "never overwritten. Grouping by kind is what makes the table usable when a defect repeats"
		+ "across hundreds of entries. A fix the rewrite itself carries cannot be left out, the"
		+ "parser having already dropped the unreadable line and the serializer writing the float"
		+ "suffix back, so it is shown as always applied with the loss named in its row rather than"
		+ "behind a box that could not be honoured, because a save manager that silently drops"
		+ "entries of a save is the failure this feature exists to avoid. A call that does not"
		+ "complete keeps the one failure idiom of the package, distinct from what the validator"
		+ "reports"
		REF @DECISION.UiSaveManagerHasOneUiErrorIdiom
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @DECISION.AGuardRefusesLocatorsTheScreenDoesNotShow
		REF @TASK.FEAT79
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the defects are presented as a table of"
		+ "the fixes to apply, ideally with a box per fix, and confirming creates a new corrected"
		+ "save file"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the display route renders the validation"
		+ "messages and the visualization area is shown only when the save carries no error, and"
		+ "the merge result is the only place that turns serialized content into a downloadable"
		+ "file"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager

TASK TEST81
	TITLE "Repair a corrupted scenario fixture in the save manager"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "a scenario fixture is generated carrying a float gauge written without its decimal suffix"
		+ "and an unreadable entry line, and the validator rejects it"
	SPEC "the save manager shows that fixture as repairable, and confirming yields a file the"
		+ "validator accepts"
	SPEC "a scenario fixture is generated whose section count is unsupported, and the save manager"
		+ "shows it as not repairable"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT80
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	RATIONALE "The repair is a flow across three engines, files, blobs and downloads, where the"
		+ "package has no layer below end to end; the scenario is what covers it. The fixtures are"
		+ "declared in the generator and replayed byte for byte by the guard, never copied from a"
		+ "real save, so no real player name and no real Steam account identifier reaches them and"
		+ "the corruption they carry is built on purpose rather than found. Two fixtures are needed"
		+ "because the two outcomes of the feature are opposite: one save that the round trip mends"
		+ "entirely, one whose section count hides everything else. The scenario asserts what the"
		+ "screen shows, the presence and the location of what is offered, never the sentence a"
		+ "rule produced, and it changes the UI for nothing but its own sake"
		REF @DECISION.ScenarioFixturesAreGeneratedAndReplayedByAGuard
		REF @DECISION.AUiScenarioAssertsWhatTheScreenShows
		REF @DECISION.UiSaveManagerHasNoComponentTestLayer
		REF @DECISION.NoRealPlayerNameInPublicContent
		REF @PROCESS.ATestTaskChangesTheUiOnlyForItsOwnSake
		REF @TASK.FEAT80
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SOURCE "User ruling of 2026-09-21 on pull request #108: the wave delivers a repair the user"
		+ "confirms, so the scenario covers the confirmation and the file it produces"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 on the default branch: the four scenario fixtures of the package are"
		+ "generated by the fixture script and replayed by the guard, and the invalid one carries a"
		+ "single violation on one record"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager

TASK FEAT82
	TITLE "Detect the links between the objects of a save that lead nowhere"
	STATUS draft
	WAVE @WAVE.7
	DESC "drafted for memory, no research done: which links a save carries, which of them the game"
		+ "tolerates broken and what fix each defect calls for are established when the task is"
		+ "refined"
	SPEC "a link from one object of a save to another that names an identifier nothing carries is"
		+ "reported by the validator with the entry it sits in, the equipment identifier of a"
		+ "player naming no inventory being the first case"
	SPEC "each defect so reported enters the repair plan, with a fix or as not repairable"
		+ "automatically"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT80
	RATIONALE "The validator checks each entry against the schema of its section and never one"
		+ "entry against another, so a save whose player names an equipment inventory that does not"
		+ "exist is accepted today. The owner expects the repair to earn its keep on the coherence"
		+ "of the data rather than on its shape, in a second step once the minimal repair of wave 7"
		+ "is delivered. The check enters the single validator, which changes the verdict of the"
		+ "display, merge and validate flows for a save accepted today, a cost to weigh at"
		+ "refinement. A repeated identifier is no such defect, the game itself writing collisions"
		+ "between inventories and world objects; a link that leads nowhere is"
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @RULE.IdentifiersAreSharedByInventoriesAndWorldObjects
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @SECTION.Inventories
		REF @TASK.FEAT78
	SOURCE "Owner ruling of 2026-09-21 on the rewrite of the wave 7 tasks of pull request 108: the"
		+ "validator validates against a schema, the least a save fixer adds is checking the links"
		+ "between objects, an equipment identifier having to name an inventory; that part comes in"
		+ "a second step and is drafted for memory only, without further research"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

TASK TEST91
	TITLE "the axe audits of the accessibility tests replay the color rules in the dark color"
		+ "scheme"
	STATUS implemented
	SPEC "every state an accessibility test audits in the light color scheme is audited again with"
		+ "the page in the dark color scheme, against the color-contrast and link-in-text-block"
		+ "rules of axe-core alone"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/helpers/createAColorRulesAudit.ts::withRules(colorRules)"
	SPEC "the dark audits live in the accessibility tests of"
		+ "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/accessibility/, in the file of the page they audit, and run"
		+ "with bun run test:ui on the three engines; no new Playwright project and no new test"
		+ "layer"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/accessibility/overview.e2e.ts::describeTheColorRulesAuditInTheDarkColorScheme(showASaveVisualization)"
	SPEC "a violation the dark audits find is fixed in the same pull request; no rule is silenced"
		+ "and no element is excluded"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/styles/shell/shell.css::.overview-pages a"
	SPEC "@DECISION.AUiTestIsEitherAScenarioOrAnAccessibilityTest states that the color rules of"
		+ "the axe audit are replayed in the dark color scheme, anchored on the dark audits"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::are replayed on"
		REF @DECISION.AUiTestIsEitherAScenarioOrAnAccessibilityTest
	RATIONALE "check:contrast reads the token pairs of colors.css in both themes but sees nothing"
		+ "of the rendered DOM: the download link of the merge result passed the catalog at white"
		+ "on --primary and was caught by the axe audit at 3.87:1, its fill derived from the token."
		+ "The accessibility tests delivered by pull request 213 audit every page against WCAG 2.0,"
		+ "2.1 and 2.2 A and AA in the light scheme only: no test sets a color scheme, and the dark"
		+ "theme is the prefers-color-scheme: dark block of colors.css, so the fills derived by"
		+ "color-mix in buttons.css and home.css have never been rendered under a check in that"
		+ "theme. The rules outside the color category read the DOM and ARIA, which the theme does"
		+ "not change, hence the color rules alone. Playwright sets the scheme per test with"
		+ "test.use({colorScheme: 'dark'}) and AxeBuilder narrows the rules with withRules."
		+ "Rescoped with the owner on 2026-09-29: the task delivered by pull request 121 asked for"
		+ "an investigation reported in the pull request body and a change picked from it, which"
		+ "required an interactive session; pull request 213 settled the adoption of axe and the"
		+ "catalog decision records what axe sees that the guard does not, so the report and the"
		+ "choice are dropped, the task can be delivered by a wave agent, and its type follows the"
		+ "pull request that delivers it. The time the dark audits add is read in the pull request"
		+ "body: the scenarios job of the UI tests workflow went from 1 min 50 to 4 min 11 between"
		+ "the master runs of 2026-09-27 and 2026-09-28, pull requests 204 and 213 both landing in"
		+ "between"
		REF @DECISION.ColorTokenPairsMeetWcagAaByCatalog
		REF @DECISION.AUiTestIsEitherAScenarioOrAnAccessibilityTest
		REF @DECISION.UiScenariosArePlaywrightSpecsOnThreeEngines
	SOURCE "The DESC of the task delivered by PR 121"
		PR 121
	SOURCE "Owner ruling, 2026-09-26: WCAG A and AA rules, color rules only in the dark scheme,"
		+ "violations fixed"
	SOURCE "Owner rescoping, 2026-09-29, after pull request 213 delivered the light-scheme audits:"
		+ "no report, no choice, the dark scheme alone remains"
		PR 213
	DELIVERED_BY 237

