	RATIONALE "Both violations are the same issue type: its sentence and its location reach the"
		+ "view as the infrastructure wrote them. Seven places word a sentence today: the section"
		+ "count and the unreadable line in shared-save-processing, the entry count, the schema"
		+ "violation, the float serialization and the file extension in the infrastructure of"
		+ "core-mapping; the presenter shows the detail as is and resolves the section name from"
		+ "the index and the format release. Each sentence becomes a code and the data it names,"
		+ "one code per sentence, so the structure code that carries two sentences today splits,"
		+ "and shared-save-processing declares the codes of its parse errors as it declares those"
		+ "of its warnings; the text of every sentence is kept, so the CLI specs and the UI"
		+ "scenarios pin the refactoring. The text of the schema validator says how a violation was"
		+ "detected, not what is invalid, so each constraint the section validators report is an"
		+ "issue of its own and the presentation words it as the validator did. The section index"
		+ "stays in the issue beside the name because the location shows both, the decision on"
		+ "locations having refused the label alone; the format release leaves the issue, the name"
		+ "being what it served to resolve. The fallback on a bare index has no case left: the"
		+ "section count is checked before any located issue exists, so every located issue belongs"
		+ "to a known format and its name resolves. The task follows the domain rules task, which"
		+ "changes the issues the validator port reports"
