	AFTER @TASK.REFACTOR161
	AFTER @TASK.REFACTOR162
	WAVE @WAVE.14
	DELIVERED_BY 238
	PRIORITY high
	DESC "outside the numbered violations of the audit"
	RATIONALE "A JSON table imported by a module is a database read by that module: the"
		+ "instructions rule data_reached_through_a_port places such a read in an infrastructure"
		+ "adapter behind a port of application/ports, and the owner ruled that the tables are"
		+ "external to the packages reading them, as a database is. The data- package is the driver"
		+ "of that database: its row types and selectors answer which rows and which value, by key"
		+ "or by order, and interpret nothing, so that the lookups shared-save-processing and the"
		+ "adapters share are written once; a rule naming a business outcome, resolving a declared"
		+ "version among others, stays in the domain. The port declares its own types so that a row"
		+ "type, the shape of the table, reaches neither the domain nor the application, the"
		+ "adapter translating. Seven tables exist today: the game releases, read by"
		+ "shared-save-processing; the energy levels, those of release 2.004, the planet names and"
		+ "the optimizer configuration, read by domain/ of core-mapping; the world object labels,"
		+ "read by presentation/; and the legacy terrain layer properties, read by no module and"
		+ "only validated, which move all the same. The packages are cut by the domain the tables"
		+ "serve, the energy tables kept together because the table of a release is validated"
		+ "against the energy table and both feed one rule. The labels follow the same flow,"
		+ "controller, use case, port, adapter, response, presenter, rather than a shortcut into"
		+ "presentation. The JSON Schemas stay in scripts/validate-tables/ and each package names"
		+ "its tables in its validate:tables script until the guard task that follows discovers"
		+ "them. The tables move before the release rules task, which then puts the releases behind"
		+ "a port of its own, implemented with the selectors of data-save-format, instead of"
		+ "splitting the table between the domain and shared-save-processing. The wiki keeps the"
		+ "dependency matrix as the state of the project at implementation time, a trace that"
		+ "survives a pause during which the instructions evolve; the instructions rule on general"
		+ "statements is amended for it by the pull request that adds the package kind. The task"
		+ "follows the reader port task, which leaves the composition root instantiating only, so"
		+ "that the adapters are wired there once, and the decoding task, which rewrites the inputs"
		+ "of the entities this task hands the table values to, so that the two changes do not meet"
		+ "in a rebase"
		REF @TASK.REFACTOR163
		REF @TASK.REFACTOR161
		REF @TASK.REFACTOR162
		REF @TASK.CHORE169
		REF @DECISION.AValueTableIsAJsonFileBesideTheModuleThatReadsIt
	SOURCE "Owner ruling during the refinement of REFACTOR163, 2026-09-29: a JSON value table is a"
		+ "database, external to the packages that read it and read behind a port; the data-"
		+ "package provides the read contract, row types and selectors"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling during the refinement of the task, 2026-09-29: four data- packages cut by"
		+ "the domain the tables serve, the energy tables together; the port declares its own"
		+ "types; the guard discovers the tables of the data- packages in a task of its own; the"
		+ "task follows the decoding task"

TASK CHORE169
	TITLE "chore(guards): validate:tables discovers the tables of every data- package"
	STATUS implemented
	SPEC "every JSON value table of a data- package has its JSON Schema beside it, under the"
		+ "table's own name, and bun run validate:tables finds every table of every data- package"
		+ "by that schema: a table is any .json file of a data- package outside node_modules that"
		+ "is neither its manifest, nor a tsconfig, nor a schema, and adding a table or a data-"
		+ "package changes neither the script nor a manifest"
		IMPL "scripts/validate-tables/validate-tables.ts::TABLES_PATTERN"
		IMPL "scripts/validate-tables/validate-tables.ts::isTable"
	SPEC "a table of a data- package with no schema of its name beside it fails bun run"
		+ "validate:tables"
		IMPL "scripts/validate-tables/validate-tables.ts::has no schema beside it"
	SPEC "no package declares a validate:tables script, the root script running the discovery once"
		IMPL "package.json::\"validate:tables\": \"bun scripts/validate-tables/validate-tables.ts\""
	SPEC "a schema several tables share, the one of the energy levels of a release first, is"
		+ "written once in its package and reached from the schema of each table's name, so that no"
		+ "rule of the rows is stated twice"
		IMPL "packages/data-energy/energyLevelsByRelease/2.004.schema.json::$ref"
		IMPL "scripts/validate-tables/validate-tables.ts::readSchema"
	SPEC "a schema names another table relative to itself, never from the repository root, the"
		+ "schema of the energy levels of a release naming the energy levels table so"
		IMPL "packages/data-energy/energyLevelsOfRelease.schema.json::\"table\":"
			+ "\"energyLevels.json\""
	SPEC "AValueTableIsAJsonFileBesideTheModuleThatReadsIt is rewritten in place: its line on"
		+ "scripts/validate-tables/schemas/ and its rejection of a schema beside its table gone,"
		+ "the schema beside its table stated with the shared schema and the relative reference,"
		+ "the one directory of schemas beside the script rejected in its turn, its anchors naming"
		+ "the code as the task leaves it; every DATATABLE names its schema at its new path,"
		+ "check:anchors passing"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/decisions.awawa::DECISION"
			+ "AValueTableIsAJsonFileBesideTheModuleThatReadsIt"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-specification/datatables.awawa::packages/data-energy/energyLevelsByRelease/2.004.schema.json"
		IMPL "package.json::check:anchors"
		REF @DECISION.AValueTableIsAJsonFileBesideTheModuleThatReadsIt
	AFTER @TASK.REFACTOR168
	WAVE @WAVE.14
	DELIVERED_BY 240
	PRIORITY medium
	DESC "outside the numbered violations of the audit"
	RATIONALE "The tables task lists the tables of each data- package in its validate:tables"
		+ "script, as the packages do today; once every table lives in a data- package, the guard"
		+ "can find them by the schema beside each, so that a new table or a new package is guarded"
		+ "without a line added anywhere. The instructions rule"
		+ "data_package_holds_tables_and_selectors places the validation of a table in its package,"
		+ "which the schema beside the table satisfies. The schema sits under the table's name so"
		+ "that the discovery needs no manifest; a table whose rows share a schema with others, the"
		+ "table of a release, keeps a schema of its own name that reaches the shared one, so that"
		+ "a new release adds a table and a one-line schema and describes its rows nowhere. A"
		+ "schema naming another table relative to itself keeps the data- package readable without"
		+ "the layout of the repository, the guard resolving from the directory of the schema. The"
		+ "task carries a medium priority: it fixes no numbered violation, but it closes the move"
		+ "of the tables, which leaves each package naming its own tables until the guard discovers"
		+ "them"
		REF @TASK.REFACTOR168
	SOURCE "Owner ruling during the refinement of REFACTOR168, 2026-09-29: the validation script"
		+ "scans the data- packages, finds the schemas and validates the tables, so that a new"
		+ "data- package needs no change of the script"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling during the refinement of the task, 2026-09-29: a release table keeps a"
		+ "schema of its own name reaching the shared definition; a schema names another table"
		+ "relative to itself; priority medium"

