		+ "sentences, not the type that crosses. The owner ruled wider than the presenters: only"
		+ "the infrastructure imports another workspace package, a type included, which departs"
		+ "from the instructions rule third_party_isolated_in_infrastructure as it stands, allowing"
		+ "type-only imports of a shared- package in domain and application; the rule is amended in"
		+ "the instructions, not derogated here. The guard is the one REFACTOR163 adds against"
		+ "runtime imports, widened to types and to every layer but the infrastructure, so that one"
		+ "guard states the refusal; this task carries it because it is the last to remove an"
		+ "import. It follows REFACTOR163 and REFACTOR162 before it, which take the runtime imports"
		+ "and the save format records out of the domain, REFACTOR164, which reduces SaveParseError"
		+ "and the validation issues to a code and its data so that the responses are built once"
		+ "from that shape, and REFACTOR166, after which a controller spec runs against a test"
		+ "double of its use case factory and needs no save content from"
		+ "shared-save-processing/testing. It precedes REFACTOR165, which then carries the merge"
		+ "warning of the domain in MergeSucceededResponse, and through it DOCS167. It carries high"
		+ "rather than critical because no domain type crosses. The review of PR 234 ruled that the"
		+ "domain says what is invalid in a save and the infrastructure how it is detected, so the"
